NAME
       chroot - run a command or shell with another directory as /

SYNOPSIS
       chroot NEWROOT [COMMAND [ARGUMENT...]]

DESCRIPTION
       chroot starts COMMAND (an interactive shell when none is given) with
       NEWROOT as its root directory: inside it, / means NEWROOT, and
       nothing outside can be reached by path. Only root may do this.

       On the RHCSA you meet it when you reset a lost root password. The
       rescue environment (rd.break on the kernel command line) mounts the
       real system at /sysroot; chroot /sysroot makes it your / so that
       passwd changes the real /etc/shadow.

EXAMPLES
       Reset the root password from the rd.break shell:

           mount -o remount,rw /sysroot
           chroot /sysroot
           passwd root
           touch /.autorelabel
           exit
           exit

       touch /.autorelabel makes SELinux relabel the files at the next boot,
       because the new /etc/shadow was written without a proper label.

SEE ALSO
       passwd(1), fixfiles(8), bootup(7)
